  "id": "COMPOUND:12871 - PROTEIN:1235",
  "verbalization": "SB-1578 is implicated in the target of multiple compounds, all of which are cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors. These inhibitors are known to modulate cellular processes by targeting cyclin-dependent kinases, which are involved in cell cycle regulation and other biological functions. The evidence suggests that SB-1578 interacts with Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1, which in turn is targeted by compounds such as 5,7-Dihydroxy-2-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-4-oxo-4H-1-benzopyran-3-yl 6-deoxy-alpha-L-mannopyranosyl-(1->2)-[6-deoxy-alpha-L-mannopyranosyl-(1->6)]-D-glucopyranoside, (Z)-3-(3,4-Dihydroxyphenyl)Prop-2-Enoic Acid, and Khonklonginol F. All these compounds are known to interact with potassium channel subfamily K member 9, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of potassium channels. The integration of these pathways implies that SB-1578 may influence potassium channel activity, potentially affecting cellular signaling and homeostasis. The evidence supports a direct relationship between SB-1578 and Potassium channel subfamily K member 9, mediated through the target of cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitors.",
